# Leaves for DOS, as a player does: Esc for the disc menu, E for Exit to DOS, and Y when it asks if you are sure.
# Start then wipes the program's code (WipeProgram), puts the screen back in 80-column text, prints its parting
# message, "Thank you for playing ELITE - Have a nice DOS!", empties the BIOS's key buffer and ends (int 20h), 0.2 s
# after Y. That happens in the end step (GameLogic/Replay.h): the last step of a replay that runs the machine, and
# the only one in which the program may end, as it must. The digest after it reads what the program left: its data
# and the text screen.
wait 0.5; key space; wait 3.5      # any key: the credits, then the status screen
key Escape; wait 0.3               # the disc menu
key e; wait 0.3                    # Exit to DOS: Are you sure (Y/N)?
